      "archaeologicalRemains": "notvisible",
      "details": "<p>ToposText writes: \"<b></b> Foundations of a fortification of large squared local blocks were found approximately 2 km NW of Agios Georgios (NW of Neapoli, Voion). Sherd scatter, looted tombs, and wheel ruts suggest this was a settlement, possibly Aphroditia/Aphrodisias of Lakonia. Nothing visible at place marked on Anavasi Monemvasia map, and museum guard believes site was mostly destroyed by modern cultivation.\"</p>",
